## 00907 PATIENT=1 DOCTOR=2
1: My periods have been really heavy for several months now, and I'm sick of it. ~ cc s1
2: I'm sorry, that sounds exhausting. How many days do you bleed for? ~ s1
1: Seven or eight days. The first three are the worst. ~ s1
2: How often do you need to change a pad on the heaviest days? ~ s1
1: Every hour, sometimes more. I've bled through at night twice. ~ s1
2: Are the periods regular, or all over the place? ~
1: Regular. Every twenty-eight days, like clockwork. ~
2: Any pain between periods, or bleeding after sex? ~ n1
1: No. Neither of those. ~ n1
2: Do you have any allergies to medicines? ~ a1
1: No, I don't have any allergies. ~ a1
2: Any other medical problems, or anyone in the family with similar bleeding? ~ h1
1: My sister had fibroids removed. That's all I know. ~ h1
2: What do you do for work, and how is it affecting you? ~ so1
1: I'm a teacher. I'm on my feet all day, and I'm so tired I can hardly think. ~ so1
2: I'm going to check your pulse and pressure and weigh you. ~
1: Okay. ~ pause=12
2: Pulse 88, blood pressure 112 over 70, temperature 36.6, oxygen 98 percent, breathing 16. ~ v
1: Is the pulse high? ~
2: A little quick, which can go with tiredness from blood loss. Let me look at your eyes and press on your tummy. ~
1: Go on. ~ pause=15
2: Your inner eyelids look pale, and your tummy is soft with no lumps. ~ x1 x2
1: Pale means anaemia, doesn't it? ~
2: It can. That's why I'd like a blood count and iron levels today. ~ p1
1: Fine. ~
2: And I'd like a scan of the pelvis, to look at the womb for fibroids or polyps, given your sister's history. ~ p2
1: When would the scan be? ~
2: I'll ask the department to book it within two weeks. You'll get a letter. ~
1: Will I have treatment today? ~
2: Not until the bloods and scan are back. I don't want to guess what is causing it. ~
1: I understand. ~
2: If you soak through a pad every hour for several hours, or feel faint, come straight to the emergency department. ~ c1
1: I will. Thank you, doctor. ~
2: I'll see you once I have the results. ~
